# With -u from a folder holding a copy of a Bloodborne save (<folder>/bloodborne/user/savedata) and
# PS_FRAME_STATS=1: past the title, Continue, then the hunter stands where the save left them. The
# frame rate is the mean of the last 10 'Frame stats' lines (the 50 s before the end):
#   grep '^Frame stats' LOG | tail -10 | awk '{s+=$3} END {printf "%.1f FPS\n", s/NR}'
# Run it alone (another game on the machine moves the result by several percent) through
# tools/regress.sh -t tools/regress/perf.txt -n bloodborne -u <folder>.
60 shot
62 press cross
70 press cross
90 shot
150 shot
155 end
